//@version=5
indicator("UCTPROBE_VW_W4_SESSION_DEFAULT_DAYS", overlay = false)

// W4 T3, row W4-T3a. A SESSION WITH NO DAY LIST: WHICH DAYS DOES IT MEAN?
//
// The columnar lane refuses a session with no `:days` suffix before Pine v5 ("the unsuffixed default
// was never measured on a weekend bar", `pine.js::sessionClockOf`): corpus scripts such as
// `ict-killzone` (v2: `BarInSession(sess) => time(period, sess) != 0` with "0100-0500") and
// `cm-forex-sessions-highlight-v1` write sessions with none. SPY has no weekend bar, so this needs a
// 24x7 symbol. The sibling `-v4.pine` is the same probe under `//@version=4`.
//
// No zone argument anywhere: the session and `dayofweek` are both read in the exchange's zone, so
// the grade is independent of what that zone is.
//
// Grade: row N1 against DOW. A session with no day list that means every day reads 0 (in) on
// Saturday (DOW 7) and Sunday (DOW 1); one that means Monday-Friday reads 1 (na) there.
//
// ⛔ CAPTURE: BITSTAMP:BTCUSD 60 (>= 400 bars, several whole weeks), inputs at defaults.

isNa(t) => na(t) ? 1 : 0

plot(bar_index, "N0_bar_index_CONTROL")
plot(dayofweek, "DOW_dayofweek")
plot(isNa(time(timeframe.period, "0000-2359")), "N1_na_no_day_list")
plot(isNa(time(timeframe.period, "0000-2359:1234567")), "N2_na_every_day_CONTROL")
plot(isNa(time(timeframe.period, "0000-2359:23456")), "N3_na_monday_to_friday_CONTROL")
